libraryPreparationPreflight.agent_guidance:
Keep the generated `testImplementation "org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion"` dependency as-is, but add a capability resolution rule to the test project's build.gradle so Gradle picks the org.hibernate.orm variant instead of failing on the capability conflict introduced by 8.0.0.Beta1's Gradle module metadata:

configurations.all {
    resolutionStrategy.capabilitiesResolution.withCapability("org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial") {
        def ormCandidate = candidates.find { it.id instanceof ModuleComponentIdentifier && it.id.group == 'org.hibernate.orm' && it.id.module == 'hibernate-spatial' }
        if (ormCandidate != null) {
            select(ormCandidate)
        }
    }
}

Verified in an isolated scratch Gradle project (not in this repo) that this rule alone turns the failing compileClasspath/testCompileClasspath resolution into a clean one; plain extra testImplementation dependencies or excludes do not fix it.
